# Local-only developer profiling tool. It opens a caller-supplied report path
# (sys.argv) — a legitimate CLI argument on an engineer's own machine, not a
# web-facing input — and self-aborts under SERVER_MODE. Excluded from Cycode
# SAST to avoid a false-positive "unsanitized user input in file path" finding.
devtools/npe_render_probe.py

# Local-only developer tool that rebuilds the smoke test's performance fixture
# from a demo report. Same false-positive class as above: `--source` and
# `--output` are argparse arguments an engineer types on their own machine, not
# web-facing input. The real risks were fixed rather than suppressed —
# `--output` is resolved and confined to `scripts/fixtures/` before anything is
# deleted, and npeviz filenames read out of the source `manifest.json` are
# collapsed to basenames — but the taint analysis still flags argparse reaching
# a path join.
scripts/generate_smoke_perf_fixture.py
